<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28873" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Messāna</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεσσήνη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Sicilian city, situated on the strait between
				Italy and Sicily</i>, the mod. <i>Messina</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 8, § 17</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Caes. B.
				C. 2, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7, 16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incumbens Messana freto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 194</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Another name for</i> Messene, <i>in
				the Peloponnesus</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Ach. 1, 422</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Messānĭus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., Messanic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					14, 17</span></i>
			 Merkel.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
